What: UnixConstants.java.template defines CLONE_NOOWNERCOPY (0x0002) when <sys/clonefile.h> does
  not, so the generated sun.nio.fs.UnixConstants keeps the constant.
Why on 10.9: <sys/clonefile.h> on 10.9 is Recaulk's, which declares clonefile (returning ENOTSUP)
  and CLONE_NOFOLLOW but not CLONE_NOOWNERCOPY (10.13). The value only reaches clonefile, which
  then fails with ENOTSUP and Files.copy falls back to copying.
Provenance: ours.
Exit: Recaulk's sys/clonefile.h defines CLONE_NOOWNERCOPY, then delete this patch.

--- a/src/java.base/unix/classes/sun/nio/fs/UnixConstants.java.template
+++ b/src/java.base/unix/classes/sun/nio/fs/UnixConstants.java.template
@@ -33,6 +33,9 @@
 #ifdef _ALLBSD_SOURCE
 #include <sys/attr.h>
 #include <sys/clonefile.h>
+#ifndef CLONE_NOOWNERCOPY
+#define CLONE_NOOWNERCOPY 0x0002 /* Mavergreen: sys/clonefile.h has it from 10.13 */
+#endif
 #endif
 
 /* To be able to name the Java constants the same as the C constants without
